{"title":"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(modular_arithmetic)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (modular arithmetic)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4(Polynomial_Remainder_Theorem)_fast_and_easy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4(Polynomial Remainder Theorem) fast and easy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Synthetic_Division_on_the_Entire_Polynomial)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Synthetic Division on the Entire Polynomial)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Mathletes_Corner\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Mathletes Corner</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solutions_2_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solutions 2 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the sum of all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/b/b3be44477b1c4728ab06d90fde978271a2a909a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" /> divides the product <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/4/c54306333a248d99cf853188c02ce2096a78fee5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3(n + 3)(n^2 + 9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/9/da9b928bb42f575cf2909b09364ebf15ad854153.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3(n+3)(n^{2}+9) }{n+2} \\in \\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"169\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/e/64eb4cfb241adf9f91192f3f6955150dba1a772e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Rightarrow \\frac{3(n+2+1)(n^{2}+9) }{n+2} \\in \\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"224\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/5/9551a2468370b5683dad484cb93a9d9908e339dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Rightarrow \\frac{3(n+2)(n^{2}+9) +3(n^{2}+9)}{n+2} \\in \\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"288\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/0/7a00df69260789ddf7e2328a2c8556554e59fcd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Rightarrow 3(n^{2}+9)+\\frac{3(n^{2}+9)}{n+2} \\in \\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"231\" height=\"42\" /> \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/6/1a69eb5c77225c4b6e94203f1afa1dc5c82f9504.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Rightarrow \\frac{3(n^{2}-4+13)}{n+2} \\in \\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"176\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/a/98aad2ded68128ad196f983cffbdbfbf53bb318f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Rightarrow \\frac{3(n+2)(n-2)+39}{n+2} \\in \\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"225\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/6/1f6e3d02580807a5232cc9d3c25c8dde7d41f8bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Rightarrow 3(n-2)+\\frac{39}{n+2} \\in \\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"193\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/3/f23c7e9d3d835c311f206b21206b389b4c57f706.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Rightarrow \\frac{39}{n+2} \\in \\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"105\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/b/b3be44477b1c4728ab06d90fde978271a2a909a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" /> is positive, the positive factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/5/e058d401a1b942f106f081ff1fcca8a8b1d42a7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$39$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/5/e058d401a1b942f106f081ff1fcca8a8b1d42a7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$39$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/5/56584f0779cf04f3f0d66161f78cb2175bd832c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/9/78916550838bd31d66e4cdefbc366edb11fd00bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$37$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is positive, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/6/c766f9fce6070981e62f805a7cf7294baed4498e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/9/78916550838bd31d66e4cdefbc366edb11fd00bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$37$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/1/a31091209088e514cfa6b0c481c4d86f532a5d34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 11 + 37 = \\framebox{049}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"152\" height=\"24\" /> is the correct answer\n</p><p>～<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Tonyttian\">Tonyttian</a>\n</p><p>~ Edited by <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Aoum\">aoum</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We observe that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/6/1f6e3acd481bacb78f324773254902e3a08d848f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/0/a70670f99b13b346e700d7fec74ab5b49061d4af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> share no common prime factor, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/6/1f6e3acd481bacb78f324773254902e3a08d848f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/4/3c48122fc92147256ea22a2b3325c29404bb5fd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3(n+3)(n^2+9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"21\" /> if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/6/1f6e3acd481bacb78f324773254902e3a08d848f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/f/7df905c0ab4a094d5f4836edbc9f09ba137033c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3(n^2+9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>By dividing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/0/ae066b23ddb149c7f670e05b5c80e77863a06cc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3(n^2+9)}{n+2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"79\" height=\"42\" /> either with long division or synthetic division, one obtains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/f/a3fa8899a3ea8af4f61d974a4d70647aa6c957f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3n-6+\\frac{39}{n+2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"122\" height=\"40\" />. This quantity is an integer if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/6/2e6aaf5d2a72600d5518f8a616b9f46976e620df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{39}{n+2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"48\" height=\"40\" /> is an integer, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/6/1f6e3acd481bacb78f324773254902e3a08d848f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" /> must be a factor of 39. As in Solution 1, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/2/6b27fb768da0b0323665eb5a96aad1f00b1d78e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\in \\{1,11,37\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"115\" height=\"20\" /> and the sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/b/d6b8af8111c12dfcef0b504649333e872c721ec2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{049}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~scrabbler94\n</p>\n<pre> NOTE: If you don't observe that it divides if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/6/1f6e3acd481bacb78f324773254902e3a08d848f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/f/7df905c0ab4a094d5f4836edbc9f09ba137033c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3(n^2+9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"21\" /> you can still do synthetic division by expanding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/4/3c48122fc92147256ea22a2b3325c29404bb5fd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3(n+3)(n^2+9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"21\" /> into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/8/0e8a071dcf8ee515f70c7cbf0815f5b7b7492b22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3n^3+9n^2+27n+81$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"171\" height=\"18\" /> and get the same remainder. -unhappyfarmer\n</pre>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28modular_arithmetic.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(modular_arithmetic)\">Solution 3 (modular arithmetic)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (modular arithmetic)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let's express the right-hand expression in terms of mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/b/b3be44477b1c4728ab06d90fde978271a2a909a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/7/1d7c155114e3e908e9905bb76ff4b9f1a6f1dd70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\equiv 3 \\pmod{n + 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"150\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/a/a0af95985ce72f5f93aeb4764d9b40afdb556f44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 3 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{n + 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"183\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/8/5f82177056c9ec54061f86435c065574e8cf48a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2 + 9 \\equiv 13 \\pmod{n + 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"199\" height=\"21\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/d/fddf715aa7dd2df6caa1253e3ac2fb101dc73680.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2 - 4 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{n + 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"190\" height=\"21\" /> with a quotient <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/8/438ca8cfe4ef1f8af9be1b9ba6670a87cced8f11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n - 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/c/7bca927d85666f51a71b62ceb86136f4a31c54ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3(n + 3)(n^2 + 9) \\equiv 3(1)(13) \\pmod{n + 2} \\equiv 39 \\pmod{n + 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"473\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>This means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/c/3dc8c053d6dd8cf05f99da85bdd5546b4aa62c20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$39 = (n + 2)k \\pmod{n + 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"216\" height=\"20\" /> where k is some integer.\n</p><p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/b/b3be44477b1c4728ab06d90fde978271a2a909a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" /> is positive, meaning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/d/91d1a485b724983fc7496cafb6d183fe9c46ee90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 2 \\geq 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/b/b3be44477b1c4728ab06d90fde978271a2a909a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" /> is one of the factors of 39, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/3/d63e965b240cfcae57d3a66c46324acdcd7cb670.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 2 = 3, 13,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"17\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/5/e058d401a1b942f106f081ff1fcca8a8b1d42a7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$39$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/b/74bad5d5d283c268ee46c25c0a784fff63c2c6a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 1, 11,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"17\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/9/78916550838bd31d66e4cdefbc366edb11fd00bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$37$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>The sum of all possible <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/2/e426a522c4daf63ebbddedfc7d69c4a2a6385c6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 11 + 37 = \\boxed{049}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"155\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~Sohcahtoa157\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4.28Polynomial_Remainder_Theorem.29_fast_and_easy\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4(Polynomial_Remainder_Theorem)_fast_and_easy\">Solution 4(Polynomial Remainder Theorem) fast and easy</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4(Polynomial Remainder Theorem) fast and easy\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/6/1f6e3acd481bacb78f324773254902e3a08d848f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" /> to be a divisor, the remainder needs to be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/6/1f6e3acd481bacb78f324773254902e3a08d848f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" />. Using polynomial remainder theorem, we can plug in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/a/62a76677add1d246708c86edfc7c4b8a40184914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/5/e058d401a1b942f106f081ff1fcca8a8b1d42a7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$39$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> as our remainder. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/6/2e6aaf5d2a72600d5518f8a616b9f46976e620df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{39}{n+2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"48\" height=\"40\" /> is an integer only when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/f/97fb6d0b1e3ed9ca62c71171b036f9f4a4eaa7b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 1, 11, 37$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"99\" height=\"17\" />. Hence, the sum of all possible <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/2/e426a522c4daf63ebbddedfc7d69c4a2a6385c6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 11 + 37 = \\boxed{049}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"155\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~AncientKarnivore\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Synthetic_Division_on_the_Entire_Polynomial.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Synthetic_Division_on_the_Entire_Polynomial)\">Solution 5 (Synthetic Division on the Entire Polynomial)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Synthetic Division on the Entire Polynomial)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/a/01af2f8d21f98c06af670776d8b82885088eaef4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3(n+3)(n^2+9)\\]\" width=\"127\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/1/c0190f6e3d85750b52974a3b4fa79a81a093ccc9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3(n^3 +3n^2 +9n + 27)\\]\" width=\"171\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/7/75701d60b7d749ebe20a28fdd755b86a7d03ee93.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3n^3 + 9n^2 + 27n + 81\\]\" width=\"167\" height=\"17\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/f/c7f2640d9541c9f70d35873b3daba8a02c54cf41.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n+2 \\ | \\ 3n^3 + 9n^2 + 27n + 81\\]\" width=\"225\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f4d4300f81f2cf0460a248f43a00aa555b11657.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{array}{r|rrrr} -2 &amp; 3 &amp; 9 &amp; 27 &amp; 81 \\\\    &amp;   &amp; -6 &amp; -6 &amp; -42 \\\\ \\hline    &amp; 3 &amp; 3 &amp; 21 &amp; \\boxed{39} \\end{array}\\]\" width=\"194\" height=\"64\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/2/a72c71b25f175c14d9e40d8f78d91d0e3371ebe2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n+2 \\ | \\ 39\\]\" width=\"75\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/4/d14b0ce8e98234f44027accb1afb2b28d7cb187a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n + 2 = \\not{1}, 3, 13, 39 \\ : \\ n \\in \\mathbb{Z}^+\\]\" width=\"226\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/a/83a224c0496f4b9500700abe395b8c8a8e089666.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n = 1, 11, 37\\]\" width=\"96\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/0/e009b4e285473050f52cee2463ca6a82ab0e5eb1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum n = 1+11+37 = \\boxed{\\mathbf{49}}\\]\" width=\"210\" height=\"26\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Mathletes_Corner\">Video Solution by Mathletes Corner</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Mathletes Corner\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WYyDe_VyvvQ\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WYyDe_VyvvQ</a>\n</p><p>~GP102\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solutions_2_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solutions 2 by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solutions 2 by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=98hzWL-cUvk&amp;t=6s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=98hzWL-cUvk&amp;t=6s</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II\" title=\"2025 AIME II\">2025 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2025 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2025\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"